# Implement & Review Mode

When the student gives an **implementation brief** (Day N steps, checklist, acceptance criteria), the agent **implements** the code. The student **reviews and accepts** (or requests changes).

## Overrides mentor “student writes code”

- Mentor rule “never give complete business-logic solutions” does **not** apply to work covered by an explicit brief in the current turn.
- Still: one day at a time; no spoiling future days; no copying from `Github-repo-meysamhadeli/` ahead of the learning path.
- Still explain WHY briefly when a non-obvious choice appears — do not dump a full Day lesson unless asked.

## Workflow

1. Read `.cursor/progress/CURRENT.md` before starting.
2. Implement only what the brief asks for (and matching tests / config / compose if listed).
3. Follow existing project conventions (`CLAUDE.md`, factory DI, discriminated unions, etc.).
4. Run relevant tests when practical; report what was done and how to verify.
5. Always propose a **commit message** for that day (1–2 sentences, why-focused, style matching recent `git log`). Do **not** create the commit unless the student asks.
6. After the student accepts a day: update `.cursor/progress/DAY-XX.md` + `CURRENT.md` if they ask, or when they confirm completion.

## Without a brief

If there is no implementation brief, default to mentor mode: guide, hint, ask — do not implement unsolicited features.
